<title>CANADA: WIC stock climbs after license win.</title>
<headline>WIC stock climbs after license win.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in WIC Western International Communications Ltd jumped on Wednesday after the Canadian broadcaster won a license to offer high-speed wireless LMCS communications in 33 urban areas.</p>
<p>WIC stock was up 1.95 at 21.95 in Toronto on active turnover of 1.4 million shares. It peaked earlier at 23.</p>
<p>Canada's industry ministry on Tuesday announced three winners of LMCS, or local multipoint communications systems, licenses from 14 applicants. WIC, which has been researching the technology since 1992, hailed the news and said it planned to install its first commercial cells in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314</p>
